hi Alex,

 if you have a function like this:

f(t) =   a*t + b*t^2 + c*t*x   and you want to compute the optimal value of t you take derivatives:

df/dt = a + 2*b*t + c

so you see the coefficient of the interaction term appears as a constant so it shows up in the optimal value of t as follows:

 t_{opt} =   -(a+c)/(2*b)

regards
andy

